AB  - The term “DevOps predictions” is used in this paper only to refer to the ability to predict DevOps adoption maturity in software organizations. The paper presents a machine learning model for predicting the level of DevOps adoption maturity in software companies. This model assesses readiness based on three key dimensions: cultural alignment, technical infrastructure, and operational resilience. This method enables an organization’s overall ability to adequately deploy and maintain DevOps practices. This paper presents a machine learning-powered pipeline for predicting DevOps readiness in software companies, helping support strategic planning and digital transformation. The proposed method boasts high predictive power and reliability thanks to the application of several ensemble learning techniques and, most importantly, a voting regression model. The model’s $\mathbf{R}$-SQ coefficient was 0.99, and its error statistics were very low (MAE $=0.04$, RMSE $=0.04$), demonstrating the model’s high effectiveness in predicting organizational patterns and readiness indicators. The research combines technical performance analysis and an implementation-based tool to measure DevOps maturity. These findings suggest that machine learning can improve decision-making and guide organizations toward more successful DevOps adoption.
ER  - 

