AB  - CI/CD pipelines are essential to modern DevOps practices, but remain vulnerable to build failures, unstable tests, and operational failures, the manual diagnosis of which is costly and difficult to scale. Recent work demonstrates the contribution of artificial intelligence to build failure prediction, log anomaly detection, unstable test analysis, and large language model-guided remediation. However, these contributions remain largely fragmented and rarely cover the entire lifecycle, from proactive prediction to remediation. This article offers a synthesis of a set of representative works and an integrated conceptual framework that links prediction, log analysis, root cause analysis, and guided remediation. It also highlights several gaps in the research, including the lack of shared benchmarks, cost and latency constraints, and the security and reliability challenges of large language model-based approaches.
ER  - 

