AB  - Industrial environments handling hazardous chemicals require rapid and reliable leak detection mechanisms to ensure safety, environmental protection, and operational continuity. Conventional leak detection systems are largely hardware dependent and reactive, offering limited scalability and predictive capability. This paper presents NeuroShield, an intelligent cloud based alarm system for chemical leak detection that integrates machine learning with DevOps driven deployment practices. The proposed system utilizes simulated sensor data representing environmental and chemical parameters to model real-time industrial conditions. Machine learning based anomaly detection techniques classify system states into normal, warning, and dangerous categories, enabling early detection and proactive response. A cloud native architecture deployed on AWS supports scalability, high availability, and centralized monitoring, while a DevOps pipeline incorporating Docker, Kubernetes, and Jenkins facilitates automated integration and deployment. Experimental results demonstrate improved responsiveness, adaptability, and predictive performance compared to conventional monitoring approaches. The proposed framework demonstrates the feasibility of software driven, artificial intelligence enabled safety systems as a scalable and cost-effective solution for industrial chemical leak detection.
ER  - 

