AB  - To monitor the progress of DevOps tools like GitHub, there appears to be an increase in the need for tools and techniques that offerings more codes. Thus, Project boards on GitHub are currently assisting the DevOps Engineer to plan, organize and prioritize works. In GitHub, we can build projects for specific feature work, comprehensive roadmaps, and release checklists. In addition, repository content or topics of the user studies require some file format or file extension to save at the specified location user projects*. In this context, Programs, called clustering algorithms, are used to determine the natural (statistical) groupings or structures in the data. Furthermore, creating clusters based on term co-occurrence using concept clustering algorithms provides an at-a-glance view of main topics and facilitated how they are related to the GitHub projects*. In this paper, we shall use clustering algorithms in GitHub by programmed language. This paper discusses also various ways of performing clustering. The applications of clustering are found in many programming languages for unsupervised learning. Then, we will argue about the choice of the most appropriate clustering algorithm for our platform, then we build a new approach algorithm to classify programming language projects (PLP) in GitHub. The paper explores also some key issues related to machine learning and DevOps tools.
