AB  - Artificial Intelligence (AI) has become a transformative technology with impact across industries. However, operationalizing AI models is not easy. It requires considerable expertise in data engineering, software development, cloud and DevOps. It also requires planning, agreement, and the vision of how a model is going to be utilized by business applications, how it is going to be continuously trained on fresh new incoming data, and how and when a newer model would replace an existing model. This paper introduces Acumos, an open-source project that aims to make AI accessible to everyone. Acumos abstracts the infrastructure stack, enabling data scientists and machine learning (ML) engineers and other roles to work together in creating AI based solutions. It facilitates fine-grained sharing of models and provides a model marketplace solution that can also be used to discover models and create complex AI pipelines. In this paper, we focus on the capabilities of the Acumos Model Runner and the Acumos Java Client that enable a novel paradigm called Reusable MLOps to make AI and AI deployments more sustainable and have continuously trained models in production quickly and easily. We will demonstrate in this paper, how we are able to reuse the existing deployment and infrastructure to serve new AI models by hot-swapping them without tearing down the existing microservice or the underlying infrastructure.
ER  - 

