AB  - With the rapid adoption of cloud-native environments, businesses are increasingly relying on continuous deployment and autonomous monitoring to maintain agility, scalability, and system reliability. This paper proposes an intelligent automation framework that enhances continuous deployment processes and autonomous monitoring within cloud-native architectures. We explore the integration of machine learning (ML) and artificial intelligence (AI) techniques to automate deployment pipelines and monitor system performance in real-time, minimizing human intervention while maximizing operational efficiency. The framework is designed to support dynamic scaling, intelligent resource allocation, and predictive anomaly detection. We evaluate the proposed solution in comparison to traditional approaches, highlighting improvements in deployment speed, system resilience, and cost optimization. Additionally, we discuss the impact of automation on cloud-native DevOps practices and the future potential of AI-driven cloud infrastructure. The experimental results demonstrate significant enhancements in both deployment cycles and system monitoring, showing a clear path for future research in intelligent cloud-native environments.
ER  - 

