AB  - This research addresses the literature on the application of Machine Learning (ML) and Reinforcement Learning (RL) to DevOps in predictive deployment and monitoring. The paper hypothesizes the Hybrid AI Model, which involves ensemble learning methods and RL to improve the decision-making process and optimization of deployment strategy in real-time. The model, implemented in TensorFlow with Keras, has shown high improvements in accuracy of deployment, efficiency, and reliability of the system. Findings indicate that the accuracy rate (92), deployment time (40) and downtime (35) decrease by 92, 40 and 35 percent respectively in comparison with traditional approaches, including Single-Model Machine Learning and Rule-Based Detection. The RL component will automatically modify the deployment strategies through constant feedbacks which will allow the system to change with dynamic environments. Although it has been successful, issues of data quality and noisy environments were experienced, which implied that it needs to be refined. In general, this paper brings out the promise of AI-based DevOps to automate and optimize the most important deployment processes.
ER  - 

