AB  - In order to assist machine learning practitioners, this paper proposes a distributed architecture that provides a full range of cloud-based services and tools covering the complete development of machine learning process. Along with features for sharing and publishing models, this covers model generation, training, validation, testing, and installation as a service. The most computationally demanding activities related to machine learning research may be handled with ease thanks to the DEEPHybrid-DataCloud architecture, which leverages distributed resources to offer smooth access to existing infrastructures. In addition to optimizing resource use, this framework offers cloud based services that let researchers publish their models for public use. It streamlines the sharing, publishing, and deployment of models by leveraging an architecture that is serverless and DevOps principles, guaranteeing developers a smooth experience. Through the use of this methodology, the framework facilitates the deployment and sharing of machine learning models by academics, bridging the gap between sophisticated computational requirements and real-world implementation. A more effective, transparent, and easily accessed machine learning workflow is made possible by DEEP-Hybrid-Data Cloud's features, which make it particularly well-suited for large-scale and computationally demanding applications. By lowering obstacles to model deployment, this strategy gives scientists more authority and facilitates increased cooperation and sharing among machine learning researchers.
