AB  - Deploying and maintaining AI models in production is often constrained by limited visibility into how code changes affect model performance. In this work, we present an integrated DevOps/MLOps pipeline that connects software development workflows with machine learning lifecycle management for mobile applications. The pipeline automatically detects if updates are derived from code or data changes, retrains models as needed, and records outcomes in a structured commit history. Each GitHub commit is linked to its MLflow run, including metrics, parameters, artifacts, and model versions. To ensure transparency and reproducibility, the system generates automated summaries with performance tables, commit-linked visualizations of accuracy trends, and artifacts bundled into the Android application. Significant result changes, whether regressions or improvements, are flagged in both plots and tables, allowing developers to trace results directly to specific commits. Additional automation manages registry models, fetches the correct version for deployment, and prunes outdated runs to maintain a clean tracking environment. We validate our approach on a mobile COVID-19 test-strip reader app, demonstrating efficient deployment of lightweight AI models on resource-constrained devices. Beyond this use case, the methodology can be applied to other settings where results must remain transparent and verifiable during continuous delivery. Our contribution is a practical framework that links DevOps and MLOps practices, making outputs transparent, visual, and reproducible across the entire CI/CD pipeline. This work offers insights for researchers and practitioners seeking scalable, transparent, and automated AI deployment in real-world applications.
ER  - 

