AB  - Artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) now represent core technologies shaping modern society; however, the fast-paced development and deployment of ML models still present significant challenges. As an adaptation of DevOps principles, Machine Learning Operations (MLOps) has emerged to provide scalable approaches for handling data and model pipelines, while ensuring the dependable deployment and continuous monitoring of ML models in production environments. Research on MLOps has progressed along multiple directions, including real-world applications, prototype development, design and architectural frameworks, methodological process improvements, benchmarking and evaluation studies, as well as the creation of novel tools and frameworks. In this study, we focus specifically on applications, as recent academic work demonstrates that MLOps practices are increasingly being adopted across diverse domains. To this end, selected recent MLOps applications are examined with respect to their domains, objectives and use cases, employed MLOps components and practices, supporting tools and frameworks, reported key findings and contributions, as well as the challenges and limitations encountered. This study aims to offer insights for researchers and practitioners seeking to understand and implement practical MLOps solutions in real-world contexts.
ER  - 

