AB  - DreamOps is an AI-powered platform for managing incidents and infrastructure automatically. It uses Anthropic Claude, a large language model integrated via the Model Context Protocol, to handle cloud-native issues. The system works with Kubernetes, PagerDuty, Grafana, GitHub, Slack, and Notion, among others. This lets DreamOps understand different infrastructure data much better. The platform handles problems in three steps: it tries to fix them on its own first, then moves to planning with human help if needed, and finally, for risky decisions, it gets final approval from humans too. It makes choices based on how confident it is about each action, keeping things safe and reliable. What sets DreamOps apart is its use of LLM- driven thinking for handling new incidents. This dynamic approach improves results dramatically. Tests showed that incidents got fixed 80% faster, and there was a 90% drop in late-night calls for engineers. Plus, the fixes became more consistent. So, DreamOps could really change DevOps by making processes smarter and partly automatic, shifting focus from reacting to being proactive and efficient.
ER  - 

